# Node.js / TypeScript (GNO)

## Style

- TypeScript strict; avoid `any` unless bridging untyped CSV/JSON edges (narrow ASAP).
- Prefer `async`/`await`; propagate errors or map to Nest HTTP exceptions at the boundary.
- Named exports for helpers; default export only when the framework expects it (e.g. Nest module class files as established).

## I/O

- Parse files (CSV/TSV/JSON) in dedicated parsers; keep services orchestration-only.
- Never commit secrets; use `.env` / local Supabase only.
- Paths: resolve from known roots; do not assume `cwd` in library code.

## Constants

- Magic numbers → `const` / `DEFAULT_*` in a types or constants module.
- Shared page sizes, thresholds, and timeouts live once and are imported.
